---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import PlaceholderBanner from '../components/PlaceholderBanner.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure"
  kicker="Transparency"
  description="How Pot and Balcony earns money from affiliate links, and why it never changes what gets recommended."
>
  <PlaceholderBanner>
    This disclosure uses placeholder wording. Replace it with your final text once your Amazon Associates account is approved,
    and have it checked against current Amazon Associates Operating Agreement rules and FTC / ASA (UK) guidance.
  </PlaceholderBanner>

  <p><em>Last updated: {SITE.legalUpdated}</em></p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    Some links on {SITE.name} are affiliate links. If you click one and buy something, I may earn a small commission at no
    extra cost to you. That commission helps pay for the site and for the gear I test.
  </p>

  <h2>Amazon Associates</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} participates in the Amazon Associates Programme, an affiliate advertising programme designed to provide a means
    for sites to earn advertising fees by advertising and linking to Amazon. <strong>As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases.</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>How I choose what to recommend</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>I recommend gear I&rsquo;ve used on my own balcony, or I say clearly that I haven&rsquo;t tested it.</li>
    <li>Affiliate commissions never decide what gets recommended, or how it&rsquo;s scored.</li>
    <li>I will say when something isn&rsquo;t worth buying, even if it has an affiliate programme.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How you can tell</h2>
  <p>
    Posts that contain affiliate links carry a notice near the top, and product boxes are labelled as affiliate links. Links
    to products are marked <code>rel="sponsored"</code> so search engines know they&rsquo;re commercial.
  </p>

  <h2>Prices and availability</h2>
  <p>
    Prices and availability change often. Any price shown is accurate only at the date given and may differ on the retailer&rsquo;s
    site &mdash; always check the current price before you buy.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Ask me anything about how this works: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
